    "summary": "High‑energy NYE show with blazing Alligator > Caution and stellar The Eleven",
    "blurb": "The December 31 performance delivers a scorching second set highlighted by an explosive Alligator > Caution transition, a thunderous rendition of The Eleven, and the rare Big Boy Pete. Jerry’s lead work shines on China Cat Sunflower and Alligator while Phil drives the jams with relentless bass power. Soundboard recordings capture the band in top form, making this one of the most compelling late‑'60s shows.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Boston Tea Party on New Year's Eve 1969 is pure, unfiltered Dead magic. The first set rolls through classics—China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider, a heartfelt Mama Tried, and a gritty Black Peter—that set the stage for a second half that truly takes off. Alligator bursts out of the gate, morphs into a double‑drum extravaganza, then snaps back into a searing Alligator > Caution sequence that showcases Mickey’s cannon‑like fills and Phil’s cello‑like bass tone. From there the band rides a high tide of improvisation through The Eleven, High Time, and a raucous Big Boy Pete before winding down with Seasons Of My Heart, the playful Dancin' In The Street and a blistering Not Fade Away. Across all available soundboard sources the mix is crystal‑clear, preserving Jerry’s soaring guitar tone, Pigpen’s organ grit, and the tight, dual‑drum propulsion that makes this night feel both historic and freshly electric.",
